DusuPay API
Developer Documentation
Comprehensive Integration Guide
1. Utility Functions
1.1 Balance Inquiry
The API allows merchants to check wallet balances for different currencies they hold.
Endpoint
GET https://sandboxapi.dusupay.com/data/wallet-balances
Wallet Types
•	MERCHANT_COLLECTION: Holds funds from collections and direct deposits
•	MERCHANT_PAYOUT: Designated wallet for disbursements
Balance Descriptions
•	available_balance: Amount available for use
•	actual_balance: Total balance (sum of all balances)
•	uncleared_balance: Amount yet to be cleared
•	reserve_balance: Rolling reserve amounts (e.g., from card transactions)
1.2 Payment Options
Before performing any transaction, merchants should query available payment options. This endpoint returns payment methods based on currency and transaction type.
Endpoint
GET https://sandboxapi.dusupay.com/data/payment-providers
Query Parameters
•	currency (required): 3-character ISO currency code (e.g., UGX, KES, GHS)
•	transaction_type (required): COLLECTION or PAYOUT
•	country_code (optional): 2-character country code for countries sharing currency
1.3 Payout Bank Codes
For all countries/currencies where DusupPay supports bank payouts, specific bank codes are required.
Endpoint
GET https://sandboxapi.dusupay.com/data/payout-bank-codes
Query Parameters
•	provider_code (required): Payment provider code from payment options endpoint
1.4 Mobile Money Operator Prefixes
All mobile money providers have specific prefixes that identify valid mobile money numbers. These prefixes come immediately after the international country code.
Key operators include MTN Mobile Money, Airtel Money, Vodafone Cash, Safaricom M-Pesa, TigoPesa, and others across Uganda, Kenya, Ghana, Tanzania, Rwanda, Zambia, and Cameroon. Full prefix tables are available in the API documentation.
1.5 Handling Notifications/Callbacks
Whenever transaction status changes (processing, failure, or success), DusupPay sends notifications to the merchant's configured callback URL.
Important Notes
•	Callbacks are sent to configured callback URLs (must be HTTPS)
•	Callbacks are JSON POST requests
•	Merchants must respond with HTTP 200 to acknowledge receipt
•	Callbacks include two verification signatures: rsa-signature and hmac-signature
•	Production IP: 161.35.164.139
•	Sandbox IP: 165.227.128.244
Callback Events
Collections Events:
•	request.failed: Request failed, could not be processed
•	transaction.charges: Communicates charges to be levied
•	transaction.processing: Transaction processing ongoing with instructions
•	transaction.failed: Transaction processing failed
•	transaction.completed: Transaction completed successfully
Payout Events:
•	request.failed: Request failed
•	transaction.failed: Processing failed
•	transaction.completed: Payout successful
1.6 Transaction Status Verification
Merchants can verify transaction status when necessary, though DusupPay sends automatic notifications.
Important Constraints
•	Status check requests denied if made less than 2 minutes after transaction initiation
•	Recommended interval: 5 minutes between status check requests
Endpoint
GET https://sandboxapi.dusupay.com/data/transaction/verify/{reference}
Transaction Statuses
•	PENDING: Logged, awaiting processor escalation
•	PROCESSING: Being processed, awaiting final status
•	FAILED: Transaction failed (reason in status_message)
•	COMPLETED: Successfully processed
•	CANCELLED: Cancelled by customer
 
2. Funds Collection
2.1 Getting Started
Collections are payments received into merchant accounts. DusupPay supports multiple payment methods including Mobile Money, Bank Transfer, Card, and Crypto.
Collection Workflow Steps
Step 1: The Collection API Request
Merchant forms collection request payload and sends to API. API responds with acknowledgement or error.
Step 2: Redirect to Payment URL (Optional)
For Mobile Money hosted page, bank, card, and crypto collections, initial response includes payment_url for customer redirection.
Step 3: Payment Instructions Notification (Optional)
For Mobile Money direct charge and Card S2S, notification sent with instructions requiring merchant action.
Step 4: Final Status Notification
Communicates final transaction status (COMPLETED, FAILED, or CANCELLED).
Cross-Currency Collections
If request currency differs from payment provider currency, API converts automatically. For example, USD request → KES payment: API converts USD to KES and credits merchant's KES balance.
2.2 Mobile Money Collection
DusupPay supports mobile money collections through two workflows:
•	Hosted Page (Recommended): DusupPay manages complete user experience and all authorization variations
•	Direct Charge: Custom merchant experience with direct API calls
Mobile Money Direct Charge
Endpoint
POST https://sandboxapi.dusupay.com/collections/initialize
Required Parameters
•	merchant_reference: Unique reference (min 8 chars) or 'auto'
•	transaction_method: MOBILE_MONEY
•	currency: 3-character ISO code
•	amount: Transaction amount
•	provider_code: From payment options list
•	msisdn: Phone number (international format)
•	description: 10-30 characters
Authorization Modes
NONE: Display instructions to customer (expect PIN prompt)
OTP: OTP sent to phone - merchant must collect and submit via /collections/authorize endpoint
Test OTP values: 123456 (success), 378961 (failure)
 
3. Payouts/Disbursements
3.1 Getting Started
Payouts are outbound fund transfers from merchant account to mobile money channels or bank accounts.
Prerequisites
Before initiating payouts, merchants must:
•	Configure payout notification URL
•	Configure payout verification URL
•	Avail funds for payout (transfer from collection wallet)
Payout Workflow
Step 1: Payout API Request
Merchant submits payout request. API responds with acknowledgement or error.
Step 2: Payout Request Verification
DusupPay calls merchant's verification URL to confirm transaction authenticity. Merchant must respond with HTTP 200 to approve processing.
Step 3: Final Status Notification
Communicates final payout status (COMPLETED or FAILED).
3.2 Mobile Money Payouts
Endpoint
POST https://sandboxapi.dusupay.com/payout/send-funds
Required Parameters
•	merchant_reference: Unique reference (min 8 chars)
•	transaction_method: MOBILE_MONEY
•	currency: 3-character ISO code
•	amount: Transfer amount
•	provider_code: From payment options list
•	account_number: Recipient phone (international format)
•	customer_name: Recipient name
•	description: 10-30 characters
 
4. Callbacks
4.1 HMAC Signature Verification
HMAC signatures enable merchants to verify callback authenticity.
Verification Steps
1. Obtain signing key from merchant dashboard
2. Extract hmac-signature header value (format: t=timestamp,s=hmac_hash)
3. Form string payload: event:merchant_reference:internal_reference:transaction_type:transaction_status
4. Create HMAC hash of payload using signing key
5. Compare resulting hash to signature header value
4.2 RSA Signature Verification
RSA signatures provide alternative verification method using DusupPay's public keys.
Verification Steps
1. Obtain DusupPay public key for environment (sandbox/production)
2. Extract rsa-signature header value
3. Form string payload (same format as HMAC)
4. Verify signature using public key and SHA256 algorithm
Note: Merchants can verify either HMAC or RSA signature, not both required.
 
5. Appendix
5.1 Merchant Account Transfers
Merchant account transfers enable fund movement between different merchant accounts and wallets through the DusupPay portal.
This process is performed via the web dashboard following these steps:
•	Navigate to Account Transfers menu
•	Click New Account Transfer
•	Select From Account and From Wallet
•	Select Receiver Account and To Wallet
•	Enter transfer amount and narration
•	Submit request for processing
5.2 Availing Payout Funds
Before initiating payouts, merchants must transfer funds from their MERCHANT_COLLECTION wallet to their MERCHANT_PAYOUT wallet. This can be done through merchant account transfers as described above.
5.3 Cross-Currency Transactions
DusupPay allows cross-currency transactions where request currency differs from payment provider currency.
How It Works
The API automatically converts request currency to transaction currency using prevailing market exchange rates. Merchant balances are updated in the transaction currency.
Example
Request: USD 100 via MTN Mobile Money Uganda (UGX)
Conversion: 1 USD = 3,800 UGX
Transaction amount: 380,000 UGX
Merchant's UGX balance credited with converted amount minus charges
Benefits
This workflow provides flexibility for merchants to bill customers in any currency while customers pay using their local payment options and currencies.
5.4 API Environments
Sandbox/Test
Base URL: https://sandboxapi.dusupay.com/
For testing and UAT before production approval
Production/Live
Base URL: https://payments.dusupay.com/
For real transactions after compliance/KYC completion
5.5 Authentication
All API requests require authentication using:
•	public-key header: Merchant account public key
•	secret-key header: Merchant account secret key (for sensitive operations)
•	x-api-version header: API version (currently '1')
 
Additional Resources
Documentation: https://developer.dusupay.com/
Postman Collection: https://postman.dusupay.com
Support: Contact DusupPay support team for assistance with integration, compliance, and go-live processes
